+  them as ``int32`` in register, deleting a caller-side ``bitcast_convert_type``
+  that XLA planned as a kLoop fusion over its own full-size temp buffer.
+  Nothing inside the kernel does float arithmetic: the resident slice is an
+  ``f32``-typed buffer whose every value is an ``int32`` monotone key, and the
+  only reason it is typed ``f32`` is that a TPU DMA matches element types
+  between source and target rather than copying bytes.
